## Why This Is Asked
Assess storage security, policy enforcement, and rollback capabilities in a practical scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy deny public network access
- Private Endpoints and VNET integration
- Managed Identities RBAC
- Secrets in Key Vault instead of config

## Code Example
```json
{
  "mode": "Indexed",
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "properties.publicNetworkAccess", "equals": "Enabled"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate rollback after applying policy?
- How would you handle temporary public access needs during migrations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end, production-grade guardrails for cross-tenant deployments in Azure, focusing on identity, secret management, policy gates, canaries, and UEBA automation.

## Key Concepts
- Workload identities and Just-In-Time access
- Azure Key Vault with per-service managed identities
- Azure Policy gates to block secrets in config
- Azure Lighthouse for cross-tenant governance
- Canary deployments with feature flags and automatic rollback
- UEBA via Azure Sentinel with automated playbooks

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "field": "type",
      "in": ["Microsoft.Web/sites", "Microsoft.AzureFunctionsJobHost"]
    },
    "then": {
      "effect": "auditIfNotExists",
      "details": {
        "type": "Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/secrets"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the policy in a non-prod environment?
- What metrics trigger the automated rollback and how are they evaluated?

## Why This Is Asked
This probes practical Azure Policy usage, Private Endpoints, tagging discipline, and CI/CD gating with rollback in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy deny public network access for storage accounts
- Private Endpoints and private DNS configuration
- Resource tagging as policy gates in CI/CD
- Rollback to last known-good ARM/Bicep template
- Monitoring and alerting via Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```json
{
  "properties": {
    "displayName": "Deny public network access on storage accounts",
    "policyType": "Regular",
    "mode": "All",
    "policyRule": {
      "if": {
        "allOf": [
          {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
          {"field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/networkAcls/defaultAction", "equals": "Allow"}
        ]
      },
      "then": {"effect": "Deny"}
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for multi-region storage and cross-tenant sharing?
- How would you test the CI gate to minimize false positives and ensure rollback works?

